<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John VI, Count of Nassau-Dillenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1536–1606</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as John the Elder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John VI, Count of Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dillenburg">Dillenburg</a>, was a brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-silent">William the Silent</a> and a leading Calvinist prince who organised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-utrecht">Union of Utrecht</a> of 1579 as stadtholder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelderland">Gelderland</a>. He founded the academy at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herborn">Herborn</a>. At his death in 1606 his lands were divided among his sons into Nassau-Dillenburg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siegen">Siegen</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadamar">Hadamar</a>, Beilstein and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diez">Diez</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-vi-count-of-nassau-dillenburg.jpg" alt="John VI, Count of Nassau-Dillenburg" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portret_van_Jan_de_Oude_(1535-1606)._Graaf_van_Nassau_Rijksmuseum_SK-A-538.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
